@startuml test-stack
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #444444
}

rectangle "Userspace" as US {
  component "envcombo-test (Rust)\n11 sequential tests, PASS/FAIL per test,\nexit code = 0 on full pass, 1 otherwise" as TEST
}

rectangle "Kernel interfaces exercised" as IF {
  component "sysfs\nraw / scale / gain / int_time\nthresholds / event enable\nbuffer + scan_elements + trigger" as SYSFS
  component "/dev/iio:deviceN\nscan records (poll + read)\nevent fd (IIO_GET_EVENT_FD_IOCTL)" as CHRDEV
  component "debugfs\n/sys/kernel/debug/envcombo-sim/regs\nside-effect-free register snapshot" as DBGFS
  component "module control\nmodprobe / rmmod\n/sys/module, dmesg" as MOD
}

rectangle "Kernel" as K {
  component "IIO core" as IIO
  component "envcombo driver\n(device under test)" as DRV
  component "i2c-envcombo-sim\nI2C adapter + ENV-COMBO model\n+ IRQ domain" as SIM
}

TEST --> SYSFS : configure & read back
TEST --> CHRDEV : samples & events
TEST --> DBGFS : assert device register\nstate (CFG, TH_*, PWR_MODE)
TEST --> MOD : load / unload cycle,\nkernel-log health scan

SYSFS --> IIO
CHRDEV --> IIO
IIO --> DRV
DRV --> SIM : SMBus byte/word
SIM --> DRV : INT (falling edge)
DBGFS ..> SIM : reads simulator state\ndirectly, bypassing the driver

note bottom of DBGFS
  The debugfs path is the harness's independent
  ground truth: driver claims (sysfs readbacks)
  are cross-checked against what actually
  landed in the device registers.
end note
@enduml
